<title>USA: Kennecott says operating at reduced level.</title>
<headline>Kennecott says operating at reduced level.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kennecott Utah Copper Corp management and contract workers were operating its strike-hit copper production plants at a reduced level, while talks between management and the labor unions were due to resume midmorning, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;The mines, the concentrators, the power plant and the refinery went out at three o'clock yesterday afternoon, and the smelter went out at ten o'clock last night,&quot; Kennecott's spokeswoman Alexis Fernandez said.  </p>
<p>All plants were now being operated by management and contract workers. &quot;Obviously it's going to be reduced production,&quot; Fernandez said.</p>
<p>She was unable to indicate what the production levels were.</p>
</text>
